ZERO OS0.7.0 - original Zero filesystem drivers and independent volumes
Verification date:2026-11-15

Final delivered disk image
build/zero.iso:17645568 bytes
SHA256:6af39753816e30ab40e77cf56af4a8edce4de20abb30ef09d722884c217a5f3b
This is a genuine ISO9660/El Torito optical image with BIOS and IA32/AMD64
UEFI boot paths. Only ISO disk images are distributed in the new package.
No IMG/VDI data disks or large private filesystem fixtures are included.
Internal FAT/padding images produced during a local rebuild are intermediate
build files. They are not renamed to ISO or presented as optical images.

Implemented system behavior
The original Zero monolithic kernel retains the pixel desktop/portrait,
PS/2/COM1 terminal and three cooperative native threads. It adds independent
A:| through Z:| volume roots, GO/go, qualified file paths, disks inventory,
four legacy ATA positions, primary MBR/GPT discovery and read-only GPT flags.
Original ext4, NTFS and Btrfs state machines support root-file reading,
creation, replacement and deletion in their explicitly bounded profiles.
The same driver source is compiled for x86-32 and x86-64. No external driver,
compiler backend, assembler, linker or guest runtime implements these features.
ROADMAP.txt separates proposed future work from completed functionality.

Compiler and source build
compiler.zero:56640 bytes
SHA256:dd2653cbb842b6e5d2778ec8ea7546460984be93376759c5725b14d37bf66f7d
bootstrap/zero:62102 bytes
SHA256:26e53cf7cafbfff584575e9f1977277af702c03ab1fa97be5d31c11ea1caca5d
kernel.zero:195387 bytes; raw64:241827 bytes; raw32:342976 bytes.
Normal build recompiles the compiler twice and requires byte-identical stages.
Both loaders, both kernels and both image builders are compiled by that own
Zero-built compiler. The BIOS component is13865 bytes within its16KiB slot;
each kernel has a384KiB image slot. BIOS validates E820 RAM for its1..4MiB
stack pool; UEFI allocates1MiB. Full source audits and source-part composition
checks are retained. The historical assembly-origin bootstrap is documented,
not erased. Current normal builds invoke no assembler or foreign compiler.
The compiler is hosted on Linux x86-64; it does not yet run inside Zero OS.

Compiler checks
- Stable seed/stage1/stage2/stage3 reproduction after the own Zero4MiB arena
  transition; source262144/output393216 boundaries and zero stdout on compile
  failures. Exact source maximum and the extra-byte rejection were exercised.
- 1107 legacy regression cases:13 expected capacity expansions, all remaining
  statuses unchanged; all322 previously successful outputs match exactly,
  allowing only the reviewed hosted arena immediate change where applicable.
- 61 current native/frontend checks; hosted native thread regression.
- 110 bit-operation assertions on host, BIOS x64 and IA32;90 real-mode
  assertions plus complete E820 enumeration with bounded-buffer checks.
- Positioned I/O tested beyond4GiB, EOF and EBADF; real fsync success/failure.
Evidence:verification/compiler-fs and review-tests/compiler-fs. Suites overlap;
these figures are not a count of distinct bugs or a proof of universal safety.

Final complete VM boots and file operations: all PASS
BIOS64: SeaBIOS, qemu64,128MiB RAM.
BIOS32: SeaBIOS, qemu64 with long mode and PAE disabled,128MiB RAM.
UEFI64: matching AMD64 OVMF firmware, qemu64,128MiB RAM.
UEFI32: matching IA32 OVMF firmware, long mode disabled,128MiB RAM.
All four use QEMU pc/TCG, standard VGA and private writable test disks.
All reached the native kernel and visible800x600 pixel desktop, accepted PS/2
commands and showed growing graphics/computation counters. All enumerated:
 A raw ZeroFS; B ext4; C NTFS; D Btrfs; E GPT ext4 marked read-only.
B/C/D were separate MBR partitions of one physical disk. E was on another.
Same-named files retained distinct contents across volumes. Every backend
passed actual guest create/save/read/overwrite/delete, duplicate refusal and
missing-file checks. GO and qualified paths selected the intended volume.
E permitted reads/listing but rejected save/create/remove and format ZERO;
the complete GPT image remained byte-identical. Healthy missing/exists errors
do not mark a filesystem unavailable; LF listings leave prompts at column0.

Persistence and external validation: all PASS
BIOS64 and UEFI64 were each shut down completely and booted in a new process
using the same final ISO and private disks. All saved foreign-filesystem and
ZeroFS contents survived; deleted files stayed absent. These read-only restart
runs left the complete writable-image hashes unchanged.
After shutdown, each mode's ext4/NTFS/Btrfs partitions were extracted and
independently checked: e2fsck -fn, ntfsfix -n and btrfs check --readonly all
returned0. debugfs, ntfscat and btrfs restore extracted exact expected bytes.
ntfsfix is a limited consistency tool, not Windows chkdsk. External checkers
and formatters are test infrastructure, never part of the Zero guest code.
Evidence:verification/fs-0.7.0/combined64 and final-three, with exact logs,
commands, expected/readback bytes and actual VM screenshots. Earlier development
runs remain labelled earlier and are not relabelled as checks of this ISO.

Driver and boundary verification
ext4:268 final assertions, including externally created files, direct/extent
mapping,128/256-byte inodes, allocation reuse/exhaustion, partition offsets,
malformed data and12 write/flush failures. A discovered cross-inode data alias
is now rejected before mutation; independent overwrite/delete reproductions
preserve the entire image hash. Ownership checks are conservative, not fsck.
NTFS: CRUD,400-byte/31-character limits, ASCII case lookup, dotfiles, MFT reuse,
external interoperability,12 write/flush failures and11 malformed/profile
refusals. Independent review hardened resident attributes, record identities,
update-sequence boundaries and LogFile metadata-alias refusal. A separate
adapter destroys volatile state across every IO and still passes CRUD.
Btrfs: CRUD, empty transitions, boundary sizes, leaf capacity/reuse, externally
populated files, nonzero partition offset;8 failed write/fsync boundaries give
externally clean old-or-new contents. Six malformed structures with valid
CRCs are refused unchanged; all root/reference/chunk bounds are checked.
Partition discovery:34 adversarial images plus3 multidisk/capacity cases,
independent partx oracle, CRC vector, read-only flags, canaries and unchanged
image hashes. Invalid tables roll back that disk's provisional inventory.
Root integration:25 path cases,23 IO-bound cases,27 independent state/safety
cases, and7 integration-wrapper corruption tests pass. They include unsafe
format attempts, empty inventories, huge indexes, IDENTIFY buffer boundaries,
read-only preservation and cross-volume failure state.
Detailed profiles/reproduction:fs/*-profile.txt and per-component reports.

User workflow and data preservation
An optical ISO is read-only. Persistence requires the user's separate virtual
hard disk; it is not silently supplied as another image format. Existing
ZeroFS disks are preserved. New blank primary-master disks require explicit
format ZERO before file creation. That command cannot format a foreign or
partitioned volume or a phantom descriptor after failed discovery.
Additional ISO-only and new-blank-disk VM checks are recorded under
verification/fs-0.7.0/iso-only. See its results for the exact workflow evidence.
The original local/Drive data disk contents were not replaced or formatted.
Original raw SHA256:c730241fb30f5516867c751006951a2878f360319195ee975411a05f040f27e8
Original VDI SHA256:7f58fb36c934405757da797ca65f2dddef3858e69107f43e2cae59d14c89bc5f
Older downloadable non-ISO disk files are preserved separately from the new
ISO-only distribution. Upgrading the ISO does not replace a user's data disk.

Practical limits
This is an early experimental OS. File operations use flat root names<=31
ASCII bytes and contents<=400 bytes. ext4 requires a clean single-group4KiB
profile without a journal; NTFS uses resident files/existing metadata capacity
and unused formatter journal pages; Btrfs uses one-device SINGLE chunks and
leaf-only inline-file trees. Default modern volumes, Windows journals,
compression, snapshots/RAID and other unsupported features may be refused.
There is no general filesystem repair or arbitrary power-loss guarantee.
Threads cooperate on one CPU in shared kernel memory. No preemption, SMP,
protected user processes, application loader, network or AHCI/NVMe/USB storage
is implemented. VirtualBox-compatible boot structures/settings are supplied,
but native VirtualBox execution and physical hardware remain unverified here.
No claim is made that all possible bugs have been eliminated.
